  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to a Class Sui Generis (HMO - house in multiple occupation) with associated cycle and refuse storage.\r",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be implemented in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rExisting Location and Block Plan - EX-L001\rProposed Location and Block Plan - PR-L001\rProposed Ground Floor Plan - PR-P001\rProposed First Floor Plan - PR-P002\rProposed Loft Floor Plan - PR-P003\rProposed Roof Plan - PR-P004\rProposed Front and Rear Elevations Plan - PR-E001\rProposed Side Elevation 1 - PR-E002\rProposed Side Elevation 2 - PR-E003\rProposed Section AA - PR-S001\rProposed Perspective View - PR-PE001\r\rOther documents submitted with the application\rFire Statement\rDesign and Access Statement\rHMO Management Plan\rHighways Proforma\rWaste Management Plan\rTransport Statement\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a sui generis House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 8 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining room shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation, details of secure, covered, and policy-compliant cycle parking shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, in consultation with the Highway Authority. The provision shall be conveniently located and directly accessible from the public highway without the need to pass through internal living spaces and shall be designed in accordance with the London Plan and London Cycle Design Standards. The approved facilities shall be provided prior to occupation and retained thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure adequate, safe, and accessible cycle parking provision is delivered and to promote sustainable modes of transport, in accordance with the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) 2024, London Plan (2021)  Policy T5 and relevant local plan policies."
  ],
